WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.539 --> 00:00:04.410
Lines spilled out into the street as fans
flocked to their nearest cinema to watch the

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:09.380
culmination of a decade of Marvel movies when
Avengers: Endgame finally arrived in theaters,

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:14.320
and judging from the reaction on Twitter,
the vast majority left more than happy.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.460
Warning: Spoilers ahead!

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.520
Filmmaker and self-professed fanboy Kevin
Smith got to attend the Endgame world premiere

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.220
with his daughter, Harley Quinn Smith.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.780
Yes, the man loves comics.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:29.300
Unsurprisingly, the Mallrats director absolutely
loved the movie, and he was eager to share

00:00:29.300 --> 00:00:29.900
that fact.

00:00:30.320 --> 00:00:34.830
Taking to Twitter afterwards, Smith predicted
that Endgame was going to smash box office

00:00:34.830 --> 00:00:35.460
records.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:37.700
"3 hours later and I'm shook!

00:00:37.940 --> 00:00:40.360
My God, Avengers: Endgame is beyond epic!

00:00:40.740 --> 00:00:44.800
It's everything you hope it will be and more,
an absolute Marvel Studios marvel!

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:47.940
And I'm pretty sure it will make all the money
ever printed!

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:50.140
Loved it and would watch again instantly!"

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.620
The hype surrounding Avengers: Endgame was
so huge that it would have been considered

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:58.760
a disappointment if was anything short of
the best superhero movie ever made.

00:00:59.330 --> 00:01:03.780
Fortunately for Marvel and everyone involved
with the picture, it was exactly that, at

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:08.400
least according to Emmy-nominated producer
and film critic Scott Mantz, who tweeted,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:13.650
"INCREDIBLE!! brings the entire MCU to a rousing,
exciting, deeply moving and wholly satisfying

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:14.260
conclusion!

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.500
It's a *BEAUTIFUL* film!

00:01:16.680 --> 00:01:18.500
Fun, smart, clever, BRILLIANT!

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:20.980
Perfect blend of action, heart and humor!

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:23.060
This is as good as it gets!

00:01:23.180 --> 00:01:24.760
Greatest superhero movie EVER!"

00:01:25.960 --> 00:01:30.720
With a runtime of three hours and one minute,
Marvel ran the risk of dragging out proceedings

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.840
somewhat, but if anything, three hours and
one minute wasn't enough.

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:38.820
The film hurtles by as loose ends are tied
and sacrifices are made, culminating in a

00:01:38.820 --> 00:01:41.040
battle of truly epic proportions.

00:01:41.240 --> 00:01:45.120
After the time-traveling Avengers finally
manage to bring the Infinity Stones back to

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:49.720
the present, Thanos arrives to wipe them and
the rest of humanity out for good.

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:53.490
One thing's for sure, the final act of the
movie really sticks with you.

00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.160
YouTube star NoahJ456 tweeted,

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:57.820
"I can't stop thinking about it.

00:01:58.060 --> 00:02:02.320
I think the last hour of Avengers: Endgame
was the greatest hour of film ever to be shown

00:02:02.320 --> 00:02:03.320
on the big screen."

00:02:03.960 --> 00:02:09.340
CinemaBlend events editor Eric Eisenberg describes
himself as a "film and comics obsessive" in

00:02:09.440 --> 00:02:13.730
his Twitter bio, meaning he's the kind of
guy who's particularly hard to please when

00:02:13.730 --> 00:02:15.400
it comes to superhero movies.

00:02:15.560 --> 00:02:19.740
Judging from the tweet he sent out after seeing
Endgame for the first time, Marvel exceeded

00:02:19.749 --> 00:02:21.609
expectations with this picture.

00:02:21.609 --> 00:02:26.260
"This can't be understated: Avengers: Endgame
is everything you want it to be and more.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:28.020
I am absolutely floored.

00:02:28.200 --> 00:02:32.820
A perfect reflection on the last 11 years
that pays off everything in the best way possible.

00:02:33.100 --> 00:02:36.400
Without question my new favorite Marvel Cinematic
Universe film.

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.000
Stunned."

00:02:37.740 --> 00:02:40.280
Character limits mean nothing when you've
got a good meme.

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:45.239
Twitter users were in good form when Endgame
was released, with MCU fans using images and

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:48.980
movie clips to convey the emotions that their
words simply could not.

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:54.900
One user by the name of RIPeterParker posted
a screenshot of Chadwick Boseman's King T'Challa

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.790
visiting his father in the Ancestral Plane
and confessing that he's not ready to move

00:02:58.790 --> 00:02:59.600
on without him.

00:02:59.800 --> 00:03:01.140
With the image, they wrote,

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:05.580
"Me staying in my seat and refusing to leave
the cinema after the credits rolled because

00:03:05.600 --> 00:03:08.430
I'm far too attached to these characters and
this story."

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.000
"I am not ready to be without you."

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:15.520
Other users have been poking fun at the fact
that Marvel has urged people not to spoil

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:18.940
the movie, posting what they're calling "spoilers
without context."

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:23.019
These range from beer bellies and rats to
cheeseburgers and tacos.

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:25.120
If you've seen Endgame by now, you get it.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:29.980
The word "epic" is probably thrown around
a little too liberally in the world of pop

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:33.800
culture, and the word was used a lot on Twitter
following the premiere of Endgame.

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:38.420
Was this just fans doing what fans do and
going overly crazy over something they love,

00:03:38.420 --> 00:03:40.180
or is Endgame truly epic?

00:03:40.540 --> 00:03:45.219
According to novelist and veteran reporter
Anthony Breznican, it most certainly is.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.280
In his estimation,

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:47.800
"Epic is the word.

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:51.660
Epic multiplied by a decade of emotion, excitement
and investment.

00:03:52.060 --> 00:03:53.060
This is the payoff.

00:03:53.340 --> 00:03:57.320
It left me with a full heart, but one I had
has some scars on it.

00:03:57.540 --> 00:03:59.520
Those are the strongest kind, after all."

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:04.340
While many have been trolling Avengers fans
with wild and elaborate fake spoilers, some

00:04:04.341 --> 00:04:08.769
people have broken the golden rule and revealed
big details from the movie on Twitter.

00:04:08.769 --> 00:04:12.720
We're going to dive into those big spoilers
right now, so this is your last chance to

00:04:12.720 --> 00:04:15.320
keep Endgame a secret if you haven't seen
it.

00:04:15.689 --> 00:04:19.720
Matter of fact, you may do well to stay off
the Internet entirely, because charmingly

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:23.120
blunt tweets like this one are definitely
making the rounds:

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:29.140
"Iron man dies, Natasha Romanoff dies, Captain
America gets old (technically implied dead)

00:04:29.140 --> 00:04:34.660
Thor is fat, Gamora is now alive and Loki
is also alive, Valkyrie is now the ruler of

00:04:34.660 --> 00:04:36.470
Asgard, Thanos disappears.

00:04:36.470 --> 00:04:37.620
Tony Stark has a daughter.

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:40.580
Bruce Banner and Hulk live as one so it's
smart Hulk."

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:41.540
And, yeah.

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.680
That pretty much sums the whole thing up.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:48.760
It happened with Josh Brolin's Thanos after
Infinity War, but this time out, Mark Ruffalo's

00:04:48.760 --> 00:04:50.690
Hulk was Twitter's bizarre crush.

00:04:51.160 --> 00:04:55.380
Ruffalo has played Bruce Banner and the Hulk
for years now, so what's the big deal?

00:04:55.680 --> 00:05:00.080
This time, they're one and the same, and the
result is giving some Twitter users confusing

00:05:00.080 --> 00:05:00.960
feelings.

00:05:01.260 --> 00:05:02.540
As one smitten fan tweeted,

00:05:02.880 --> 00:05:06.980
"Hey not to be predictably me, but why is
Professor Hulk so hot?"

00:05:07.420 --> 00:05:10.890
Another said that they were sticking to their
guns despite the critics, declaring,

00:05:10.890 --> 00:05:13.210
"I'm being bullied for speaking my truth!

00:05:13.210 --> 00:05:14.620
Yes, I'd smash Hulk!

00:05:15.040 --> 00:05:17.200
He's the hot professor I've always wanted!"

